---
import InsertLayout from '../layouts/InsertLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../utils/jsonld';

const jsonLd = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy', url: '/privacy' }
]);

const lastUpdated = 'September 19, 2026';
---

<InsertLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Toledo Technologies website. Learn how we collect, use, and protect your information."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  subheading={`Last updated: ${lastUpdated}`}
>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Toledo Technologies LLC ("we," "us," or "our") respects your privacy. This
    policy explains how we collect, use, and protect information when you use
    toledotechnologies.com, any subdomain of toledotechnologies.com, and any
    other site or checkout operated by Toledo Technologies LLC.
  </p>

  <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

  <h3>Information You Provide</h3>
  <p>When you contact us through our website, we collect:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name and email address</li>
    <li>Any information you include in your message</li>
    <li>Project details you share with us</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Automatic Information</h3>
  <p>
    This site loads Cloudflare Web Analytics, a measurement script served from
    static.cloudflareinsights.com. It records page views and basic technical
    detail — the page address, the referring page, browser and device type, and
    country. Cloudflare states that it does this without cookies and without
    fingerprinting visitors. We use it only to see which pages are read; it is
    not an advertising tracker and we run no ad network on this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    Like any web host, the server and security layer may also process ordinary
    request data such as IP address, browser, requested path, and timestamp for
    delivery, reliability, and abuse prevention.
  </p>

  <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
  <p>We use collected information to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to your inquiries and requests</li>
    <li>Provide services you've requested</li>
    <li>Operate, secure, and improve our website and services</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information with third parties
    for their marketing purposes. We may share information:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      With service providers who assist our operations (e.g., email delivery)
    </li>
    <li>When required by law or to protect our rights</li>
    <li>With your consent</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    We do not collect or store your card number. Card payments are processed by
    Stripe, Inc. Depending on which product you buy, a purchase may instead be
    processed by Gumroad, PayPal, Polar, or the Microsoft Store. That processor
    collects your payment details directly, under its own privacy policy, and
    passes us only what we need in order to fulfil and account for the order:
    your email address, the item, the amount, the currency, the country used for
    tax, and the brand and last four digits of the card.
  </p>
  <p>
    We use that order record only to deliver your purchase, handle refunds and
    chargebacks, and meet our tax and accounting obligations, and we keep it for
    as long as those obligations require — generally up to seven years. We do
    not sell it and we do not use it for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Form</h2>
  <p>
    Forms submit to Toledo Technologies' lead intake API at
    <code>https://eolkits.com/api/v1/lead</code>. The service stores the fields
    you submit in Toledo's operating lead database and sends the owner a
    notification email. This is durable lead capture; it is not FormSubmit and
    it is not used to add you to a newsletter.
  </p>
  <p>
    The form may also include hidden context such as the page, service track, or
    subject that brought you to the form. That context is used to route the
    inquiry. If you prefer not to use the form, email
    <a href="mailto:hello@toledotechnologies.com"
      >hello@toledotechnologies.com</a
    > directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We implement reasonable security measures to protect your information.
    However, no internet transmission is completely secure. We cannot guarantee
    absolute security of data transmitted to our website.
  </p>

  <h2>Your Rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Request access to personal information we hold about you</li>
    <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
    <li>Request deletion of your information</li>
    <li>Opt out of any marketing communications</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use advertising cookies, and the analytics described above sets
    none. The gatefold homepage uses browser
    session storage to remember that you opened the sleeve during the current
    tab session; that value is not used to identify you or build a profile.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-Party Links</h2>
  <p>
    Our website may link to external sites. We are not responsible for the
    privacy practices of other websites. We encourage you to read their privacy
    policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our website is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly
    collect information from children.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy periodically. We will post changes on this page
    with an updated revision date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Us</h2>
  <p>For privacy-related questions or requests, contact us at:</p>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:hello@toledotechnologies.com"
      >hello@toledotechnologies.com</a
    >
  </p>
</InsertLayout>
